implementationPlan.note:
moe-agent.ps1 runtime, edited in place with Edit; BOM ef bb bf kept. ParseFile reports 0 errors on pwsh 7.6.9 and PS 5.1.26100.
(a) A new section after Stop-MoeSeatVm, 'Verified-local check dispatch (CQ-M07s)'. It sets $script:CheckDispatchGraceSec=120, CheckDispatchProcess, CheckDispatchCode, and adds:
- Resolve-MoeCheckDispatchCli. Default <root>\local-runner\check-dispatch.mjs. MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH is honored only when unprotected; when protected, R's PATH_IGNORED warning goes to stderr verbatim.
- Find-MoeReplyKey (a case-sensitive key lookup) and Get-MoeCheckDispatchVerdict, an exact port of check_dispatch_verdict:
  - read at most 1048577 bytes; strict UTF-8;
  - drop one trailing \n; any \n or \r left, or text not starting with '{', is refused;
  - stopped.code or code must match [A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}\z; environment= is added only for moe-local-vm-v1:[0-9a-f]{64}\z;
  - taskId and candidateId must be -ceq and results an array, then rc!=0 gives NOT_PASSED, and empty results give REPLY_INVALID;
  - FileNotFound gives NO_REPORT; any other read error throws, and the caller maps it to REPLY_INVALID.
- Stop-MoeCheckDispatch [GraceSec]. It waits the grace, then runs taskkill /T /F /PID <recorded pid> (by pid only, never by name), waits 5 s, disposes, and clears the record last.
- Invoke-MoeCheckDispatchChild:
  - removes the 5 credentials plus GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE and GIT_COMMON_DIR, and restores them in finally;
  - prints the cyan 'Post-flight: owed checks in check VMs: task <id> candidate <cand>' line;
  - runs Start-Process node <cli> --project $projectPath --task $preflightTaskId --commit $Frozen.Commit with stdin an empty file, stdout to a file and stderr to a discarded file, -NoNewWindow;
  - polls WaitForExit(1000) up to the bound; a timeout gives Stop 0 and TIMEOUT. rc is $p.ExitCode, and a non-int rc counts as 1;
  - its finally calls Stop with the 120 s grace (only an interrupted wait still holds the record), then removes the temp files.
- Invoke-MoeCheckDispatch. Rel prints the existing NOT_TOP line and sets code MOE_WORKTREE_PROJECT_NOT_TOP. A bound that Get-MoeLandLeaseBudget refuses gives TIMEOUT_INVALID; no node or no CLI leaf gives UNAVAILABLE. PASS prints green '[OK] check VMs passed every owed check of candidate <cand>.'. Anything else sets CheckDispatchCode and writes one stderr '[WARN] MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_REFUSED: <verdict>' line.
(c) L6 in Invoke-MoeWorktreeRounds. A new branch runs when configuredGate, a task id and Test-MoeStrongLandingTask all hold: New-MoeFrozenCandidate (commit-tree M -p B, so the dispatched commit is the frozen one; no second commit-tree, per the G8 text ban), then Send-MoeCandidate, then Invoke-MoeCheckDispatch. Any failure gives MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE with R's exact Msg '... was not frozen, recorded and passed by the check VMs (<code or no dispatch>)'.
(d) The legacy 'if ($Settings.configuredGate) {' became '} elseif ($Settings.configuredGate) {' with its body byte for byte unchanged.
(e) The outer finally adds 'try { Stop-MoeCheckDispatch $script:CheckDispatchGraceSec } catch {}' right after Stop-MoeGateChild (round-2 G).
DEVIATION from the step text: Start-Process plus $p.ExitCode replace '& node' plus $LASTEXITCODE and the pipe encodings. A time bound and a recorded pid need a process object. Stdout goes straight to a file, so no pipe encoding is involved.
SMOKE, in process on both engines with the real fake: pass gives PASS; crash gives NO_REPORT; garbage and two-lines give REPLY_INVALID; not-passed gives NOT_PASSED; code gives RUNNER_NOTHING_OWED; TIMEOUT_SEC=0 gives TIMEOUT_INVALID; a missing CLI gives UNAVAILABLE. On a timeout, hang gives TIMEOUT in 2.2 s with the fake dead. In 8 dispatches no credential reached the child, and the env was restored. A runspace Stop() mid hang-hard waited the 3 s grace, then the fake was dead and the record cleared.
The verdict table matches Python on both engines, D and E included. Known engine leniency: ConvertFrom-Json accepts single quotes, /* */ comments (pwsh 7) and a trailing U+00A0, which Python refuses. JSON.stringify never produces any of them.
Out-of-scope bug filed: task-e444f6ae2fc94efda2899ba723cf5c4b (no Windows-deliverable graceful stop in check-dispatch.mjs, so a timed-out ps1 dispatch is force-killed and can leak its VM).

implementationPlan.description:
postflight-vm-route.ps1 rows, 1:1 with CQ-M07r's postflight-vm-route.sh rows (the port contract from step 1). Reuse R's scripts/tests/postflight-fake-check-dispatch.js through node; never add a second fake.

Add a new section (for example `[strong gate]`) after the landed [strong intent] G-rows, so a peer's appended rows merge cleanly:
- canary: the host qualityGate is a command that would write a witness file. Under strong, the witness is absent, and the target moves only after the fake passes;
- one row per non-pass case (non-zero exit, a stopped report, RUNNER_NOTHING_OWED, RUNNER_DEPENDENCIES_UNDECLARED, a missing CLI, a crashing CLI, an unparsable reply): each is MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE with nothing published, and the line byte-identical to the sh row's expected line;
- an environment id is printed; a malformed one is not;
- MOE_CHECK_DISPATCH_PATH is ignored under MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1, with the warning;
- the legacy control: a non-strong completion still runs the host gate.

Keep the landed [vm candidate] R1-R9 and [strong intent] G1-G8 rows unedited.

Follow mem:decision-ps1-harness-pin-inline-wrapper-block and mem:gotcha-wrapper-slice-tests-execute-text. Mind PS 5.1 encodings in fake output (mem:gotcha-windows-python-text-mode-crlf-in-node-tests): compare decoded strings, never raw bytes.

implementationPlan.note:
New [strong gate] section in postflight-vm-route.ps1 (+273/-0, purely additive; Invoke-SgSections called after Invoke-VmjSections; R1-R9, G1-G8 and every other existing row unedited). It reuses R's postflight-fake-check-dispatch.js through node; there is no second fake.
Rows:
- E2E 1:1 with sh (real wrapper, fake seat VM, codex worker, all 5 credentials exported):
  - SG-pass and the SG-legacy/SG-observe host controls;
  - SG-nonzero, stopped, nothing-owed, undeclared, crash, unparsable, env (the line names the id), env-malformed (code alone), missing and timeout (<60 s);
  - SG-protected (exactly one PATH_IGNORED line, the override never printed).
  - Assert-SgRow ports sg_check assertion by assertion, including the byte-exact REFUSED and MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_GATE lines.
- SGV: sh's whole verdict table, plus R's round-2 D (pass + two newlines) and E (results object at rc 0), plus V-missing. D, E and G are ported from their descriptions; R's round 2 has not landed.
- SGU U1-U6 run in process. U7 is a runspace Stop() mid hang-hard: the grace is honored, the fake is dead and the record cleared.
- G: static check of the four consecutive outer-finally lines, plus a behavioral run of the exact wrapper line against a recorded hang-hard fake.
- SG8: static order strong-if < Invoke-MoeCheckDispatch < elseif < Invoke-MoeFrozenGate < intent.
Port deviation: where sh expects one check-dispatch-term, ps1 expects 0 TERMs and a dead pid (U5, U7, SG-timeout).
Results:
- The full harness prints PASS postflight-vm-route.ps1 on pwsh 7.6.9 and PS 5.1.26100 (MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=360).
- Mutants were run in a scratch copy outside the checkout, and each fails at the intended row:
  - PASS also accepting NOT_PASSED fails at SG-nonzero;
  - env anchor \z changed to $ fails at V-env-malformed "<id>\n";
  - Test-MoeStrongLandingTask always $false fails at the SG-pass canary ("the qualityGate ran on the host");
  - the outer-finally stop line dropped fails at G.
Harness gotchas fixed along the way:
- the comma binds tighter than + inside @(), so concatenated SGV elements needed parentheses, and a 4-field guard now catches that;
- $X and $x are the same variable;
- a one-row scriptblock answer unrolls to a PSCustomObject, which has no .Count on 5.1, so every call site wraps in @().
